---
import { site } from '@/config/site';
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy"
  description="What the Cherry Creek website does, and does not do, with your data."
  intro="A plain description of how this website works. It is a small community site, and it is built to collect as little as possible."
>
  <h2>What this website does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It has no accounts, forms or comment sections, so there is nothing for you to submit.</li>
    <li>It does not set cookies or use your browser's local storage.</li>
    <li>It does not use analytics, advertising or tracking scripts.</li>
    <li>
      It does not load fonts, scripts or images from other companies. Everything is served from this
      site.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What happens when you visit</h2>
  <p>
    Like any website, loading a page means your browser sends a request that includes your IP
    address and basic browser details. Requests to this site pass through Cloudflare, which provides
    its network security and delivery, and then reach the server that hosts the site. Either may
    keep technical logs of requests for security and troubleshooting.
  </p>

  <h2>Live server status</h2>
  <p>
    The status card asks this website's own server whether the Minecraft server is online. It shows
    only the online state, the number of players, the player limit and the game version. It never
    shows player names or IP addresses, and your browser never contacts the Minecraft server
    directly.
  </p>

  <h2>Copying the server address</h2>
  <p>
    The copy buttons write the server address to your clipboard when you press them. The website
    cannot read what is on your clipboard.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other services</h2>
  <p>
    The{' '}
    <a href={site.mapUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      interactive map
    </a>{' '}
    and
    <a href={site.discordUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Discord
    </a>{' '}
    are separate services that open in a new tab. Nothing from them is embedded here. Discord has
    its own privacy policy, and playing on the Minecraft server itself is not covered by this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Ask the community administrators on{' '}
    <a href={site.discordUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Discord
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</Page>
